From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:20:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] keystore2: permission checks without SELinux (cfg
 atl_no_selinux)

With cfg atl_no_selinux the caller context comes from its binder uid
(apps: untrusted_app, AID_SYSTEM: system_server), getcon is keystore's
own context and check_access reads the system/sepolicy grants for the
keystore2 and keystore2_key classes (private/app.te:164,
private/system_server.te:1057,1071). The keystore2_key label backend
has no keystore2_key_contexts: every Domain::SELINUX namespace lookup
is denied (PermissionDenied, as for any mapped domain on a device),
never a panic in permission.rs's LazyLock. libselinux is never called.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hosts without an Android SELinux policy]
Patch-Reason: binderd sends no SID, so every check fails without calling_sid; host kernels have no Android policy (AppArmor label, or a Fedora policy judging Android contexts) and libselinux's disabled path grants apps every permission
---
